# CSE450 Translation of Programming Languages
## Lecture 11:Generating and Running WebAssembly Text (WAT)

---
### The Generated WAT Program
[full] @(70, 150) {$code, w=765px, size=18px} ```
(module
  (func $CalcHypotenuse
    (param $var0 f64) (param $var1 f64) (result f64)
    (local $var2 f64)       ;; c_sqr
    (local.get $var0)
    (local.get $var0)
    (f64.mul)
    (local.get $var1)
    (local.get $var1)
    (f64.mul)
    (f64.add)
    (local.set $var2)
    (local.get $var2)       ;; Assignment result
    (drop)                ;; Unused by statement
    (local.get $var2)
    (f64.sqrt)
    (return)
  )
  (export "CalcHypotenuse" (func $CalcHypotenuse))
)
```
[explain] @(870, 180) {$note, w=330px, size=27px, color=explain} Each operator follows its operands in the emitted instruction stream.
...
[assign] @(870, 335) {$note, w=330px, size=27px, color=explain} The assignment leaves a value. The enclosing statement discards it.
...
[implicit] @(870, 495) {$note, w=330px, size=25px, color=explain} At the function’s end, the final f64 can also be returned implicitly. The later source examples omit `(return)`.
---
### How Do I Run This WAT Code?
[s1] @(84, 175) {$note, w=1112px, size=32px} **1. Convert WAT to Wasm.**
[command] @(84, 250) {$code, w=1112px, size=28px, pad=6px} ```bash
wat2wasm hypotenuse.wat -o hypotenuse.wasm
```
...
[s2] @(84, 365) {$note, w=1112px, size=32px} **2. Write an HTML file that loads the Wasm module.**
...
[s3] @(84, 470) {$note, w=1112px, size=32px} **3. Serve the files and open the HTML page in a browser.**
[serve] @(84, 550) {$note, w=1112px, size=27px, color=emp} Use an HTTP server so fetch can load hypotenuse.wasm.
---
### Installing wat2wasm
[intro] @(70, 150) {$note, w=1140px, size=30px} `wat2wasm` is part of **WABT**, the WebAssembly Binary Toolkit.
[mac] @(70, 245) {$note, w=540px, size=28px, color=emp} **macOS: use your package manager**
[maccommands] @(70, 305) {$code, w=545px, size=23px} ```bash
# Homebrew
brew install wabt

# Or MacPorts
sudo port install wabt
```
...
[linux] @(665, 245) {$note, w=545px, size=28px, color=emp} **Ubuntu / Ubuntu in Windows WSL**
[linuxcommands] @(665, 305) {$code, w=545px, size=23px} ```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install wabt
```
[other] @(70, 565) {$note, w=1140px, size=26px} Other systems: [WABT releases and build instructions](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wabt).
[source] @(70, 625) {$note, w=1140px, size=23px, color=id} Course instructions: [Project 3 tool setup](../project3.html).
% Source: web/project3.md, "Set up the tools to test your compiler".
% Verified: https://github.com/WebAssembly/wabt and https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/wabt
