### Removing Redundant Instructions
[opt0] @(70, 150) {$code, w=765px, size=19px} ```
(module
  (func $CalcHypotenuse
    (param $var0 f64) (param $var1 f64) (result f64)
    (local $var2 f64)       ;; c_sqr
    (local.get $var0)
    (local.get $var0)
    (f64.mul)
    (local.get $var1)
    (local.get $var1)
    (f64.mul)
    (f64.add)
    (local.set $var2)
    (local.get $var2)       ;; Assignment result
    (drop)                ;; Unused by statement
    (local.get $var2)
    (f64.sqrt)
  )
  (export "CalcHypotenuse" (func $CalcHypotenuse))
)
```
[explain] @(870, 175) {$note, w=330px, size=26px, color=explain} Start with the generated program. At the end of this function, the result can be returned implicitly.
...
[h1] {color=focus, thick=3, fill=none, round=0} !rect (75,481.2) (755,26.599999999999998)
[h2] {color=focus, thick=3, fill=none, round=0} !rect (75,507.79999999999995) (755,26.599999999999998)
!anim explain text This get immediately followed by drop has no effect.
...
!anim h1 hide 0.15s
!anim h2 hide 0.15s
!anim opt0 hide 0.15s
[opt1] @(70, 150) {$code, w=765px, size=19px} ```
(module
  (func $CalcHypotenuse
    (param $var0 f64) (param $var1 f64) (result f64)
    (local $var2 f64)       ;; c_sqr
    (local.get $var0)
    (local.get $var0)
    (f64.mul)
    (local.get $var1)
    (local.get $var1)
    (f64.mul)
    (f64.add)
    (local.set $var2)
    (local.get $var2)
    (f64.sqrt)
  )
  (export "CalcHypotenuse" (func $CalcHypotenuse))
)
```
!anim explain text Remove the unused assignment value and its drop.
...
[h3] {color=focus, thick=3, fill=none, round=0} !rect (75,454.59999999999997) (755,53.199999999999996)
!anim explain text The remaining set/get pair stores the sum, then immediately reloads it. Here, c_sqr has no later uses.
...
!anim h3 hide 0.15s
!anim opt1 hide 0.15s
[opt2] @(70, 150) {$code, w=765px, size=19px} ```
(module
  (func $CalcHypotenuse
    (param $var0 f64) (param $var1 f64) (result f64)
    (local $var2 f64)       ;; c_sqr
    (local.get $var0)
    (local.get $var0)
    (f64.mul)
    (local.get $var1)
    (local.get $var1)
    (f64.mul)
    (f64.add)
    (f64.sqrt)
  )
  (export "CalcHypotenuse" (func $CalcHypotenuse))
)
```
!anim explain text Keep the sum on the stack for f64.sqrt and remove the set/get pair.
...
[h4] {color=focus, thick=3, fill=none, round=0} !rect (75,241.8) (755,26.599999999999998)
!anim explain text Now $var2 is unused, so its local declaration can be removed.
...
!anim h4 hide 0.15s
!anim opt2 hide 0.15s
[opt3] @(70, 150) {$code, w=765px, size=23px} ```
(module
  (func $CalcHypotenuse
    (param $var0 f64) (param $var1 f64) (result f64)
    (local.get $var0)
    (local.get $var0)
    (f64.mul)
    (local.get $var1)
    (local.get $var1)
    (f64.mul)
    (f64.add)
    (f64.sqrt)
  )
  (export "CalcHypotenuse" (func $CalcHypotenuse))
)
```
!anim explain text The result is a compact sequence of stack instructions.
[format] @(870, 440) {$note, w=330px, size=26px, color=emp} Other WAT formats can make the same computation easier to read.
